I apologize for the oversight. I completely missed that you specifically wanted the **Single Table** approach. For an Asset Management system where you want all data in one single table with a `type` column to distinguish them, here are the corrected files.

### 1. The Root Parent Entity

**File:** `Asset.java`
This is the base class. It defines the `@Inheritance` strategy as `SINGLE_TABLE`. All children will live in this table.

```java
package com.International_Racing.Models;

import jakarta.persistence.*;
import lombok.Getter;
import lombok.Setter;

@Entity
@Getter @Setter
@Inheritance(strategy = InheritanceType.SINGLE_TABLE)
@DiscriminatorColumn(name = "asset_type", discriminatorType = DiscriminatorType.STRING)
public abstract class Asset {

    @Id
    @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)
    private Long id;

    private String assetName;
}

```

